&lt;p&gt;     12&sol;2003 - Expanded Medicare coverage for screening for early detection of colorectal cancer by adding additional fecal occult blood test (iFOBT, immunoassay-based) that can be used as alternative to existing gFOBT, guaiac-based test. Medicare coverage continues to allow one FOBT per year for beneficiaries aged 50 and over. Effective date 1&sol;01&sol;04. Implementation date 1&sol;05&sol;2004 for coverage &amp;amp; HCPCS codes and 4&sol;05&sol;2004 for frequency edits. (&lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Transmittals&sol;downloads&sol;R5NCD.pdf&quot;&gt;TN 5&lt;&sol;a&gt;) (CR 2996)&lt;&sol;p&gt;
